    "turn_idx": 50,
    "turn_text": "And so I'm a strict constitutionalist and I'm somebody that believes that if we make promises, we keep them. In fact, I gave a term limits pledge. I was one of the few that actually kept my promise on that. So that's not popular with a lot of the, you know, the country club Republicans. And so when I campaigned in 2012, I was very much skews the pun, a salmon swimming upstream, because I was fighting against all the establishment guys, and I won that election. I went back to Washington, D.C., and I got sick with what I saw. The Republicans, many of them, most of them, had turned into a bunch of wimps. John Boehner was the Speaker of the House. We promised that we were going to repeal Obamacare. And we weren't bringing the bills to the table. And so I got sick of it. And so Jim Jordan, Mark Meadows, Ron DeSantis, and I got together. We created the Freedom Caucus. And we were a pain in the butt to those Republicans that were just mouth-only Republicans. Are you pissed off? Yeah, I'm pissed off because I get sick and tired of politicians promising one thing and doing another. I've heard it all my life. And so of the people out there that I'm talking to, that I deal with, they hear these people say one thing and do another. Like Arnold Schwarzenegger, big friggin celebrity. He was gonna go and change everything. He's such a great guy, the Terminator. He ended up being a loser. He ended up being somebody that didn't keep the promises. He did not honor the promises that he made, and he was a loser. Jesse Ventura in Minnesota. We can go through all these different people that promised to be one thing and then they ended up being something",
