    "turn_text": "She's got a bachelor's and a master's in education. She's been a school teacher. Her husband is my dentist. Okay. And they live about a mile away. They have four terrific kids. The oldest is a senior in high school. And they're all outside. They love everything outside. All my family, we love shooting. We love guns. We love knives. I know it's your pack in the day. I heard somebody said, Congressman Sam, it's packing to see. You know what? And that's what I pack in today. I have a lot of favorite guns. You know, and somebody asked me one time, you know, how many guns you got? And I said, no self-respecting gun or can tell you how many guns they have. I don't know. I have a lot. I know. That's the same way. I haven't done inventory. I haven't counted them all. I've got a lot. I've got a couple of ARs. I've got a lot of hunting rifles. I deer hunt every year. I've got a lot of deer heads on my wall. I love outdoors. I love to shoot. I'd say my favorite pistol right now that I have is when I just got about eight months ago from the vault in Mesa commercial for them. I bought a Nighthawk and it's probably my favorite gun I've ever shot. I had a really nice Ed Brown that I've had for many, many years, but this Nighthawk puts it to shame. And, you know, I mean, that's probably my favorite pistol to have right now. But I have a Glock that's all tricked out and, you know, got the Trigicon Red Dot sights on it, and I love it. It's a fun gun to shoot, but nothing that compares with my new Nighawk. I love it.",
