    "turn_text": "founding fathers, they gave us the tool. It's the ninth and the tenth amendments, which say that everything not delegated to Congress is left to the people in the states. The enumerated powers are clearly enumerated. If they ain't there, then that's for the people in the states. And we've been passing unconstitutional stuff probably since Woodrow Wilson. And I believe that we need a governor that's going to stand up and fight against that encroachment. A second piece, you know, whether it's vaccine mandates or whether it's dealing with, you know, any of the crap that's coming from this administration, we need to have a governor that's going to stand up and say, you know what, I'm not going to comply with that. And one of the people I looked to was one of the guys that started the Freedom Caucus with me. He was my best friend when I was in the house. That's where I understand. They are doing things the way I want to do things in Arizona, and that is to keep the federal government at bay. And when they're not doing their job, like on the border, I believe we need to step in and do our own job, because we have a sovereign border to protect. In Article 4, Section 4 of the Constitution, it guarantees every state. that we will be free from invasion. Well, we're being invaded and we are not being protected. We have a right to stand up and protect what's ours.",
