    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/5/0/50929.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 210,
    "turn_text": "But the government, look, they made, when you go back and you look at the chronology, the evolution, after Deng Xiaoping and he wanted to open up China and Nixon, in 72 normalized the relations with China at the time. And since that time, it's just gone backward again. So the first really so-called freely elected president of China after Deng was Jiang Zemin. And they really wanted to move to a more free-market-based China and kind of relinquish some of the reins off of China. The bad thing that really happened was when this current president got elected, Xi Jinping, he's not a good person at all, and he's basically declared himself the eternal leader, and he wants to go back to full-throated communism. It's a total reversal of where they were even 10 years ago, and it's scary. China poses the biggest threat to our society by far. It's existential.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_00",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
